1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:04,840
So we move on to phase four, which is testing.

2
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:08,370
We can also call it integration and testing.

3
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:13,980
What is happening in this in this stage?

4
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:20,610
The goal is to ensure the software meets requirements.

5
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:28,110
This is where quality assurance, QA team, steps in to test the software.

6
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:37,200
All the modules of the software are brought together into a special testing environment and tested for

7
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,720
errors and interoperability.

8
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:47,040
Software developers fix any bugs that come up during this stage.

9
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:52,950
Then QA specialists test the software or its components again.

10
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:58,860
All the defects are tracked, fixed and retested.

11
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:08,490
There are different kinds of testing, functional testing, performance testing, unit testing, integration

12
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:11,310
testing, regression testing, etc.

13
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,340
Who is involved here?

14
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:16,170
Of course testers.

15
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:25,440
We can also call them QA specialists, developers as well, business analyst, project manager and other

16
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,180
stakeholders as needed.

17
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,050
So we have quite a lot of words here.

18
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,670
Let's look at them.

19
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:34,510
Goal.

20
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:37,770
A synonym is aim or objective.

21
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:42,830
So this is something that you are trying to do, something that you are trying to achieve.

22
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:51,110
So as a result, you want to have a working application, a working software that meets the requirements.

23
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:58,000
It means this is your goal. To ensure means to make sure.

24
00:01:58,010 --> 00:02:00,770
Let's jump back and look at this word here.

25
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:09,080
The goal is to ensure the software meets requirements, to make sure.

26
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:21,820
To step in means to become involved, to start doing something on the project. Module.

27
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:24,550
You can see the transcription here.

28
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:29,050
Module or component again compOnent.

29
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:34,600
The stress is here is a part of the program or the part of the software.

30
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:41,010
Bring together means to assemble, to collect, to compile.

31
00:02:41,010 --> 00:02:42,570
These are all synonyms.

32
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:55,790
A bug, the synonyms can be an error defect, a flaw, and it is of course a problem in the software

33
00:02:55,790 --> 00:02:58,780
program or it's incorrect behavior.

34
00:02:58,790 --> 00:03:01,370
We don't want to have any bugs, of course.

35
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:04,380
Let's move on.

36
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:06,990
A nice word

37
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:09,090
interoperability.

38
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:18,570
Interoperability is the ability of one system or application to interact with another system or application.

39
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:28,830
So it's the communication of two systems or two components, how they interact and how they operate

40
00:03:28,830 --> 00:03:29,610
together.

41
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:35,700
Their ability to do that. To go over means to look through.

42
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:41,910
You want to find any mistakes or bugs in your code.

43
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:44,700
So you go over your code.

44
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:57,270
To track bugs means to log and monitor bugs or errors during software testing and to log means to make

45
00:03:57,270 --> 00:04:01,740
a list of them, describe them and have them documented.

46
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:13,830
To fix bugs is to eliminate software errors or software flaws, defects. And to retest means to test again.

47
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,519
That was testing.

48
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:25,530
And we go to the next phase, which is phase five deployment.

49
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,310
Now, let's see what's going on here.

50
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:35,070
The product is deployed to the production environment.

51
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:48,210
If the customer wishes UAT or user acceptance testing is done before deployment for UAT, a replica

52
00:04:48,210 --> 00:04:54,150
of the production environment is created and the customer company does the testing.

53
00:04:54,330 --> 00:05:03,240
So user acceptance testing is something that not the development team but the customer team is doing

54
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:09,870
in order to check if the program behaves well, behaves the way they wanted.

55
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:19,390
Once they check that the product works as expected, they give a sign off to go live.

56
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:28,390
The customer may also come up with changes or enhancements to the software behavior.

57
00:05:28,690 --> 00:05:31,900
These changes are called change requests.

58
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:40,810
After they are done, the product is released to the market or deployed in the company's production

59
00:05:40,810 --> 00:05:41,710
environment.

60
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:45,710
Who is involved here?

61
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,190
Release manager.

62
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,700
Project manager.

63
00:05:49,910 --> 00:05:50,930
Developers.

64
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:51,950
Testers.

65
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:58,100
And of course, the customer and the customer's team if they want to do the user acceptance testing.

66
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,070
Now let's look at the words.

67
00:06:03,930 --> 00:06:06,510
The first word, of course, to deploy.

68
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,340
What does it mean to deploy?

69
00:06:08,370 --> 00:06:16,680
It means to make a software system available for use. Replica - an exact copy.

70
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:27,950
A sign of a sign off is a business document or it's just a confirmation from the customer that they

71
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:31,550
agree on the status of the project or goal.

72
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:38,720
It can be the end of the project phase or the end of the project, the entire project.

73
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:44,030
When the customer accepts the software product and is satisfied with it.

74
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:48,020
It means we have done everything.

75
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:49,970
We have analysed.

76
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:51,530
We have planned.

77
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:55,280
We have built the application.

78
00:06:56,570 --> 00:06:59,000
We have implemented everything.

79
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,770
We have tested everything.

80
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:04,350
And now this is the final stage of the project.

81
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:12,060
We give this product the result of the project to the customer.

82
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:17,110
The customer tests it and they say, Yes, it's good.

83
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:21,440
I accept the work and this is the sign off.

84
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:27,320
And it can be a document and official document where the person where the customer really signs the

85
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:31,760
document or it can be any other form of acceptance.

86
00:07:32,270 --> 00:07:36,050
But this is the end of the project for the Development Team.

87
00:07:38,450 --> 00:07:40,790
The next is to go live.

88
00:07:41,270 --> 00:07:49,130
To go live is the point at which code moves from the test environment to the production environment.

89
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:53,180
Therefore, it becomes available for end users.

90
00:07:55,450 --> 00:08:01,390
To come up with something is to suggest or think of an idea or plan.

91
00:08:01,390 --> 00:08:09,640
For example, the customers can come up with any other ideas after the project is done and they want

92
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,460
to change something or do something else.

93
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:23,710
Enhancement is the improvement. And release, release as a noun and to release.

94
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:31,570
So the release is the distribution of the final version of an application.

95
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:38,260
Or if we say to release, it means to distribute the final version of an application.

96
00:08:43,950 --> 00:08:52,050
And the last stage that we have here is phase six or stage six maintenance.

97
00:08:52,050 --> 00:08:54,180
We can also call it support.

98
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:58,680
What is happening here? During this

99
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:06,480
the system is assessed to ensure it doesn't become obsolete.

100
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:16,710
If any issue comes up and needs to be fixed or any enhancement needs to be done, developers take care

101
00:09:16,710 --> 00:09:17,310
of that.

102
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:22,830
This is also where changes can be made to initial software.

103
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,700
Who is involved here?

104
00:09:28,350 --> 00:09:37,020
Developers, testers, project manager, service manager and other stakeholders if needed, as needed.

105
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:39,600
Let's look at the words.

106
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:49,440
So to assess means to check and decide about the quality of something. And assessment, it means the

107
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:57,510
process of checking and considering all the information about something to make a judgement.

108
00:09:57,510 --> 00:10:01,440
So assessment is making a judgement.

109
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,310
Is it good?

110
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:13,110
Is it bad? To ensure again means to make sure. And obsolete means something old that is not in use anymore

111
00:10:13,110 --> 00:10:16,380
or that has been replaced by something newer and better.

112
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:20,280
So obsolete very generally is too old.

113
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,480
Issue.

114
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:28,510
Issue is a question or problem that needs to be solved.

115
00:10:29,290 --> 00:10:35,380
To come up is to happen to appear usually unexpectedly.

116
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:40,540
For example, some some changes come up.

117
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:48,010
The necessity to change something comes up and the development team has to react on that.

118
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:51,580
Enhancement is improvement.

119
00:10:51,580 --> 00:11:00,310
Again, we've already seen this word. And initial means first, first or original, something that was

120
00:11:00,310 --> 00:11:01,330
at the beginning.

121
00:11:04,590 --> 00:11:07,810
So that's it for software development lifecycle.

122
00:11:07,830 --> 00:11:13,630
So, again go to the quiz and check your understanding.

123
00:11:13,650 --> 00:11:15,780
Check how you've memorised your words.

124
00:11:15,930 --> 00:11:17,970
And we will move on.

